        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: ઝોકું",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ઝોકું — jhokũ — \"a nap; a nod of the head in sleep\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "બપોરે દાદાને ટ્રેનમાં ઝોકું આવ્યું. bapore dādāne ṭrenmā̃ jhokũ āvyũ. In the afternoon grandfather nodded off on the train."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "A neuter noun."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ઝોકું (jhokũ) seems to belong with the Gujarati verb jhukvũ, \"to bend\", which CDIAL lists under jhukkati, \"stoops\", a form it reconstructs (CDIAL 5399): the head bends forward as you doze. CDIAL gives no form for ઝોકું itself, so the link is hedged."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for getting around."
            }
          ]
        },
